From 1940f9e7278cc6144528485c79421d802a9b30cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:06:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] LOCAL: rockchip: rk3399-roc-pc: Restore SD card IO
 voltage in SPL

Linux switches the SD card IO supply (vcc_sdio, RK808 LDO4) to 1.8V
for UHS-I modes. The PMIC is not reset on a warm reboot, so SPL reads
the card with the pads at 3.3V and the supply at 1.8V, and loading
u-boot.itb fails with block read errors.

Enable I2C, PMIC and RK8XX regulator support in SPL and include
vcc_sdio, the i2c0 pins and the IO domains in the SPL devicetree, so
dw_mmc sets vqmmc back to 3.0V before reading the card.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-roc-pc-u-boot.dtsi    | 10 ++++++++++
 configs/roc-pc-mezzanine-rk3399_defconfig |  6 ++++++
 configs/roc-pc-rk3399_defconfig           |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-roc-pc-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-roc-pc-u-boot.dtsi
index 883d399a06a..48ad6207365 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-roc-pc-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-roc-pc-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -44,6 +44,14 @@
 	bootph-pre-ram;
 };
 
+&i2c0_xfer {
+	bootph-pre-ram;
+};
+
+&io_domains {
+	bootph-pre-ram;
+};
+
 &spi1 {
 	flash@0 {
 		bootph-pre-ram;
@@ -64,7 +72,9 @@
 };
 
 &vcc_sdio {
+	bootph-pre-ram;
 	regulator-always-on;
+	regulator-init-microvolt = <3000000>;
 };
 
 &vcc_sys {
diff --git a/configs/roc-pc-mezzanine-rk3399_defconfig b/configs/roc-pc-mezzanine-rk3399_defconfig
index 8b4d8c1b0aa..dd2ed89ba7b 100644
